WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.970
Game of Thrones Season 6 Episode 4 is out
– let’s have a look.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:09.240
At the Wall, Jon tells Edd he’s gonna go
south and “get warm”, which seems pretty

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.280
fair after the shit Jon’s been through.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.110
He’s been attacked by zombies, torn up by
an eagle, shot by his lover, strangled by

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.820
a Thenn, stabbed by Karl Tanner, beat up by
walkers, and finally fuckin murdered by his

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.270
own men – so if anyone deserves a holiday,
it’s Jon.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.820
But the vacation is delayed when Brienne,
Pod and Sansa arrive at Castle Black.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.540
Jon and Sansa haven’t seen each other since
Season 1, in fact we’ve never even seen

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.680
them talk to each other in the show or books
til now, cause they were never really close

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:40.370
– Sansa was always the lady, off doing ladylike
things, while Jon was ever the bastard, an

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.879
outsider, moping in the shadows.

00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:46.770
But now, after all that their family has been
through, their relationship means so much,

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.309
so it’s beautiful to see the two unite.

00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:53.910
Anyway Sansa wants to retake Winterfell and
wreck Ramsay’s shit up, though Jon is reluctant

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:54.910
– for now.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:58.540
But by the way – does Sansa know that Jon
died and was resurrected?

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.260
Is he not gonna bring that up?

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:04.430
Sansa has so far been separated from the supernatural
in this series, so it’ll be interesting

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:08.040
to see how she reacts when she finds out her
brother is a zombie.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.040
Anyway.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.450
Davos, Melisandre and Brienne meet and quickly
establish they’ve all got beef with each

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:16.970
another – Melisandre used blood magic to
kill Renly Baratheon, who Brienne loved.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:20.360
Brienne killed Stannis Baratheon, who Davos
and Mel were loyal to.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:25.130
And though Davos doesn’t yet know it, Mel
burned Shireen, who Davos loved like a daughter.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:28.800
So basically all these guys have reasons to
hate each other, which could possibly lead

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.990
to conflict in the future.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:35.000
Down in the Vale, we see Robin Arryn, son
of Lysa Arryn, who Littlefinger murdered a

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.810
couple seasons ago, and of Jon Arryn, who
Littlefinger convinced Lysa to murder before

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:40.810
that.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:44.100
Robin has spent a season in the care of Yohn
Royce, but that doesn’t seem to have made

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:48.240
him a better warrior – he shoulda done a
training montage like Arya.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.550
Yohn Royce is actually kind of a cool character.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.880
In the books, he’s called “Bronze Yohn”,
for the ancient bronze armour he wears, “engraved

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.500
with magic runes” . His son Robar joins
Renly Baratheon’s Kingsguard, and ends up

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:04.410
killed by Loras in a rage after Renly’s
death, and Yohn’s third son is Waymar, the

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:08.590
Watchman from Episode 1 who’s killed by
a white walker.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:12.590
Anyway Royce is Littlefinger’s biggest political
opponent in the Vale . So when Littlefinger

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:17.230
turns up, Yohn’s all like I think you gave
Sansa to the Boltons, so Littlefinger’s

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:20.120
all like I think you gave Sansa to the Boltons.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.349
Of course, Yohn is right, but Lord Robin sides
with Littlefinger – cause Petyr keeps buttering

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:26.190
him up with these gifts.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:29.520
So long as Robin’s under Littlefinger’s
thumb, there isn’t much the Lords of the

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:34.370
Vale can do against him – the falcon is
the sigil of House Arryn, so this caged falcon

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:37.890
could symbolise Littlefinger’s control of
the Vale.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.160
Also Littlefinger says he’s gonna use the
knights of the Vale against the Boltons to

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:46.610
get back Sansa – so these guys could be
instrumental in the upcoming battle for Winterfell.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:51.030
In the latest instalment of one girl, two
eunuchs and a dwarf, Tyrion negotiates a peace

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:55.629
with the cities of Slaver’s Bay, by allowing
them to slowly phase out slavery instead of

00:02:55.629 --> 00:02:58.140
straight-up banning it as Dany wanted.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:02.430
Of course, this upsets the ex-slaves, including
Grey Worm, Missandei, and the freedmen of

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:03.430
Meereen.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:07.180
But Tyrion argues that they have to make some
kind of deal or the whole situation will fall

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.860
apart – which is a great illustration how
politics works, right?

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:14.750
It’s easy to say let’s bring peace and
justice for all, but sometimes that’s not

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:15.750
possible.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.590
Sometimes, you gotta compromise, you gotta
choose between two evils.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:23.020
It’s like how Jon decided to bring wildlings
south of the Wall – that did threaten the

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:27.239
Watch, and broke their traditions and values,
but it was necessary to stop the white walkers

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:28.709
growing stronger.

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:32.990
All that said, as clever as Tyrion may be,
he doesn’t really know he’s talking about

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.049
here.

00:03:34.049 --> 00:03:37.870
Like Grey Worm says, Tyrion doesn’t know
the cultures of Slaver’s Bay, nor does he

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:42.500
know true horror of being a slave, so even
if he’s right that they’ve gotta compromise,

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.319
he may be overconfident here.

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:47.080
This uneasy peace may not last.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:50.830
Meanwhile, the Super Daario Brothers track
Daenerys to Vaes Dothrak.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.720
Daario sees Jorah’s greyscale, and Jorah
is like, nah don’t worry about this highly

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:59.560
contagious incurable fatal disease that turns
you into a zombie, it’ll be fine.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:04.019
No doubt Daario will be looking for an opportunity
to put Jorah down, cause, really, that stuff

00:04:04.019 --> 00:04:08.330
could spread – and a grey plague is the
last thing anyone needs right now…

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:13.250
Anyway, Jorah and Daario go on a super sneaky
mission to rescue Dany in Vaes Dothrak, and

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.020
it doesn’t go very well.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:19.660
Jorah seems a bit rusty in combat, maybe the
spreading stone is slowing him, and Daario

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:23.030
splatters a body with a rock, cause, stealth!

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:26.479
Dany sits through a lecture from the dosh
khaleen, then makes a friend, heads out, meets

00:04:26.479 --> 00:04:29.930
Jorah and Daario, and devises a plan.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:33.081
In King’s Landing, Margaery is still with
the sparrows – and she’s looking real

00:04:33.081 --> 00:04:36.070
fine for someone who’s been pooping in a
bucket for weeks.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:39.770
She meets with the High Sparrow, who tries
to win her over with a speech about – the

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:42.759
moral emptiness of Westerosi materialism?

00:04:42.759 --> 00:04:46.330
He seems to be speaking from the heart, but
it doesn’t convince Marge.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:50.350
Marge gets to meet with her brother Loras,
and Loras is a wreck, desperate to get out

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.710
of his dungeon, though he’s still probably
better off than where he’s at in the books

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:58.081
– in Dance, Cersei sends Loras to retake
Dragonstone, where he gets deep-fried by a

00:04:58.081 --> 00:05:02.289
pot of boiling oil – at least we’re told
that’s what happened – some fans believe

00:05:02.289 --> 00:05:05.389
that’s a lie, and he’s secretly fine – but
anyway.

00:05:05.389 --> 00:05:09.360
Tommen meets his mother and seems a bit torn
between Cersei and the High Sparrow, who he

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:11.700
had that lovely chat with last episode.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:15.430
Tommen then tells Cersei a secret that the
High Sparrow told him, and the secret seems

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:19.440
to be that the Sparrow’s planning a walk
of shame for Marge, cause that’s what Cersei

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.510
then tells Olenna and Kevan.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:25.470
She convinces them use a Tyrell army to take
out the High Sparrow.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:29.920
Olenna agrees, cause she wants to free her
grandchildren Marge and Loras, and Kevan agrees

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:34.650
in the hope of getting back his son Lancel,
the dopey kid with the funny hat from Season

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:38.430
1 who was wounded at the Blackwater and ended
up joining the sparrows.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:42.580
By the way – Jamie doesn’t seem to know
that Cersei had an affair with Lancel – maybe

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.930
he’ll find out and break up with Cersei.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:48.400
Anyway all agree to take out the Sparrow with
force, and by the looks of these shots from

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:52.300
the trailer – it looks like the Tyrells
will have no trouble overwhelming the sparrows

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.820
– or could there be more going on here?

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:57.479
We know the Sparrow’s good at manipulating
Tommen.

00:05:57.479 --> 00:06:01.681
Maybe he told Tommen his plans for Margaery
knowing that Tommen would tell Cersei, and

00:06:01.681 --> 00:06:04.479
knowing that Cersei would respond with force.

00:06:04.479 --> 00:06:08.160
Maybe this all part of the Sparrow’s plan
and he’s got something special up his sleeve

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:09.490
to deal with these soldiers.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:11.530
We’ll have to wait and see.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:15.009
Meanwhile, Theon Greyjoy returns to the Iron
Islands.

00:06:15.009 --> 00:06:20.020
Last time he came, he was a swaggering overproud
douchebag, now he’s a broken man.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:24.229
The tragedy of Theon is that all he ever really
wanted was a family.

00:06:24.229 --> 00:06:28.320
He was born a Greyjoy of Pyke, but after the
Greyjoy rebellion, he was taken as a sort

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.370
of a hostage by the Starks.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:34.759
Eddard treated him kindly, but he never felt
truly accepted , which led him to betray the

00:06:34.759 --> 00:06:39.370
Starks for the Greyjoys, but he soon found
he wasn’t accepted by them either.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:43.410
Theon has done terrible things, but only to
be loved.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:47.530
And of course, no one deserves the torture
that he suffered at Ramsay’s hands.

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:51.800
So all this just makes it sadder that his
sister’s so mad with him, for his terrible

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:56.160
choices, and for wasting her men in that failed
rescue attempt in Season 4.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.970
At first she thinks Theon now wants to claim
the Seastone Chair, but Theon says he wants

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:03.380
to support Yara in her claim to the throne
of the Iron Islands.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:08.770
It’s not clear how Theon could help – cause
the ironmen respect strength, and Theon isn’t

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:11.160
strong right now, so we’ll see how that
goes.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:15.990
Either way, we’ve got a kingsmoot coming,
an election of the new ruler of the ironborn.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:20.050
Asha and Euron both have awesome speeches
in this chapter of the book, hopefully some

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:23.010
of that will make it into the show.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:27.520
At Winterfell, Ramsay tries to be intimidating,
but Osha brings the sass – pointing out

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:31.660
that while he may flay people, at least he
doesn’t eat them, like the Thenns do, beyond

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:32.669
the Wall.

00:07:32.669 --> 00:07:36.919
Osha tries to seduce Ramsay – a tactic she’s
used before – and for a moment it looks

00:07:36.919 --> 00:07:41.220
like she might kill him, but Ramsay’s playing
her, he knows she helped Rickon escape Winterfell

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:45.720
before, so he kills her, then keeps on peeling
his apple.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:50.300
The death of Osha is further evidence that
the Umbers giving Ramsay Rickon probably isn’t

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:55.819
part of any northern conspiracy, and if it
is, the plan’s already going badly.

00:07:55.819 --> 00:08:00.410
Back at the Wall, Edd, Jon, Tormund, Pod,
Brienne, and Sansa have brunch.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:04.440
Tormund takes a fancy to Brienne, which is
adorable, then a Bolton man arrives with a

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:10.319
letter from Ramsay, demanding Sansa, and threatening
all manner of violence and rape and awfulness.

00:08:10.319 --> 00:08:13.139
In the books, this letter is known as the
“pink letter”.

00:08:13.139 --> 00:08:16.990
It arrives before Jon’s death, and there’s
lots of mystery surrounding it, like some

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:21.150
readers believe it was actually written by
Mance Rayder, who’s still alive in the books.

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:24.690
But in the show it seems more straightforward,
it’s pretty clear that the letter was written

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:27.580
by Ramsay, and delivered by a Bolton man.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:32.479
So Sansa urges Jon to ride south with the
wildlings to save Rickon and Winterfell.

00:08:32.479 --> 00:08:37.550
The numbers aren’t good – Ramsay apparently
has 5,000 men, while there are only 2,000

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:41.830
fighting wildlings, but Sansa suggests they
ask the loyal northern houses for help – so

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:45.940
maybe Davos will be sent to White Harbour
like in the books – and also we know that

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.650
those knights of the Vale are on their way.

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:52.760
So this is all laying the groundwork for a
truly massive battle, that some fans are calling

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.380
“Bastardbowl”.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:59.310
Back at Vaes Dothrak, Dany stands before the
Dothraki khals, the leaders of all the thousands

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:01.820
and thousands of Dothraki in the city.

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:05.540
Dany gives a speech about how awesome she
is, which is just kinda what she does, and

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:09.000
the Dothraki threaten rape, which is kinda
what they do.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:14.120
So Dany burns down the temple with the khals
and herself trapped inside, then dramatically

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:19.351
emerges from the flames unharmed and all the
Dothraki bow down at her feet –a lot like

00:09:19.351 --> 00:09:23.680
the end of Season 1, when Dany rises from
a pyre with her dragons.

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:27.490
This scene seems to confirm that, in the show,
Daenerys is immune to fire.

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:31.261
In the books, she’s not – Dany gets burned
in Dance , and the author George Martin has

00:09:31.261 --> 00:09:35.600
said that the Season 1 thing was a one-off
magic miracle type thing, but either way,

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:39.890
what’s interesting about this scene is what
it means for Dany as a character.

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:44.589
This is a fulfilment of Quaithe’s words,
that “To go forward [Daenerys] must go back”

00:09:44.589 --> 00:09:48.880
. Dany has gone back to the Dothraki, back
to her birth as the Unburnt, back to violence

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:50.640
and fire and blood.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:55.480
She’s spent so long compromising, chaining
her dragons, trying to peacefully rule foreign

00:09:55.480 --> 00:10:00.880
cities – this is a return to her roots,
back to being a dragon-queen.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:04.410
Which raises the question – what was the
point of the last few seasons then, if she’s

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:06.390
just going back to where she started?

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:10.020
What's the point of a character arc that loops
back to where it began, there needs to be

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:11.690
change, right?

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:16.480
Maybe Daenerys will change by going even further
in the direction of violence than she ever

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:21.390
has before, maybe she'll burn down the cities
of Slaver's Bay, cut a bloody path across

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:26.200
Essos, and arrive at Westeros not as a saviour
but as an invader with a horde of Dothraki

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:31.770
barbarians and foreign sellswords, a mad tyrant
like her father the Mad King.

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:37.710
Either way, we’ve now had both Jon and Dany
reborn this season – Jon from ice and Dany

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:38.960
from fire.

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:42.430
They both have followers thinking they’re
some kind of god, they both have red priests

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:46.980
saying they’re Azor Ahai or the prince that
was promised, the saviour of the world – however

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:51.910
this story ends, Dany and Jon will be at its
centre.

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:52.910
Thanks for watching.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:56.100
Special thanks to all the translators who
have been translating captions for these videos

00:10:56.100 --> 00:11:01.089
into Spanish, Arabic, German, Russian, French,
and more – your work is very much appreciated

00:11:01.089 --> 00:11:04.490
– if you’d like to help, link in the description.

